<title>LEBANON: Lebanon April budget deficit narrows vs March.</title>
<headline>Lebanon April budget deficit narrows vs March.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lebanon's cumulative budget deficit totalled 1,448.8 billion Lebanese pounds between January and April 1997, according to finance ministry statistics issued on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The April deficit fell to 384.192 billion pounds from 499.4 billion pounds in March.</p>
<p>The 1997 budget envisages income of 4,100 billion pounds against spending of 6,433 billion.</p>
<p>The ministry issued the following statistics (in billions of Lebanese pounds):</p>
<p>				Jan	Feb    Mar	Apr     Total</p>
<p>   Expenditures	    503.6  576.7   703.7    619     2,402.9</p>
<p>   Of which interest exp 243    180     245	263.4     932.1</p>
<p>   Revenues		  250    265     204.3    234.8     954.1</p>
<p>   Deficit		   253.6  311.7   499.4    384.2   1,448.8</p>
<p>($1=1,543.5 Lebanese pounds at end of April 1997)</p>
<p>Beirut editorial (9611) 745307 345740 602057</p>
